/P 81 0 R
/T (XGBoost performed best but explains only about 10% of rating variance. This indicates ratings are driven substantially by factors not captured by geography or visit timing alone, most likely individual subjective experience, service quality on the day, or attraction-specific factors not present in this feature set. Adding user-level historical behavior \(for example, a user's average past rating\) would likely improve this in a future iteration.)
/E (XGBoost performed best but explains only about 10% of rating variance. This indicates ratings are driven substantially by factors not captured by geography or visit timing alone, most likely individual subjective experience, service quality on the day, or attraction-specific factors not present in this feature set. Adding user-level historical behavior \(for example, a user's average past rating\) would likely improve this in a future iteration.)
